# [P2] Lemma A.66 (d = 2, m = 2): the splitter d^m -> (d, d), the Z box a (2 -> 2) of dimension d and
# the binder are the box a of dimension d^m.
# Dimensions are literal. Paper pink spiders are X spiders with their normalisation d^((m+n)/2 - 1) as scalar.
# A mixed-dimensional Z box is its definition ([P2] (2.3.3)): a Z box over the product of its leg
# dimensions, each leg through a binder or splitter whose other leg carries a pink dot.

@lhs =
    s1 = S(literal 2, literal 2)
    z2 = Z(2 -> 2, literal 2) weight{1: a}
    b3 = B(literal 2, literal 2)
    wire s1.out0 -- z2.in0, s1.out1 -- z2.in1, z2.out0 -- b3.in0, z2.out1 -- b3.in1
    inputs s1.in0
    outputs b3.out0

@rhs =
    z1 = Z(1 -> 1, literal 4) weight{1: 0, 2: 0, 3: a}
    inputs z1.in0
    outputs z1.out0

load @lhs
prove against @rhs
certificate kernel
